    "description": "My research has been in data mining in the data starved domain of software effort estimation for Dr. Menzies.  The work has focused on exploring methods to improve accuracy and represent the uncertainty of the estimate.  This has involved machine learning methods such as feature subset selection, bagging, and boosting, and the use of Monte Carlo simulation.  The research is funded by NASA's Jet Propulsion Laboratory which also hosted a summer internship where I implemented the research findings into an application.",
